    95	- **Round-1 gate.** Round 1 is the registered doubling check. Before round 2, its held-out winner (round 1's search
    96	  winner, evaluated on the evaluation seeds against the frozen reference) and both changes are compared with the
    97	  registered doubling record: exact seeds and discrete knobs, 1e-9 on continuous knobs, changes, and held-out gains, all
    98	  values finite. On a mismatch the cell stops ("stopped: round 1 differs"), no recompute is written, and the run exits 4.
    99	- **Nesting cells.** Round 1 is unchanged (the gate). From round 2 the round's incumbents add the doubled D2+H3 winner
   100	  (the report's held-out knobs) embedded in X7-SC (`embed_h3`), and the cell runs at least two rounds. Its shortfall
   101	  (better D2+H3 winner minus X7-SC evaluated gain, same seeds) is reported before (posthoc) and after (final winner).
   102	- **Pass.** A round passes when both changes against the previous round (attacker best training value; reselected
   103	  reference mean normalised profit) are below the registered threshold 0.005. Stop at the first pass; cap three rounds
   104	  (four times the registered restarts in all). Reported as "passed the registered incremental check within three rounds"
   105	  or "not passed at the cap"; this is not convergence, not optimality, and not a bound on the remaining search error.
